# DMARCReport MCP Server

[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@duocircle/dmarcreport-mcp.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@duocircle/dmarcreport-mcp)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that enables AI assistants to interact with the [DMARCReport](https://dmarcreport.com) API. Goes beyond data passthrough by providing DMARC-aware reasoning and actionable recommendations.

> **What is MCP?** [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) is an open standard that allows AI assistants to connect to external tools and data sources.

## Features

- **Full API Coverage** - Access all DMARCReport data (domains, aggregate reports, forensic reports, MTA-STS)
- **DMARC Reasoning** - Get intelligent analysis with grades, blockers, and recommendations
- **Policy Progression** - Check if domains are ready to advance from none → quarantine → reject
- **Configurable Profiles** - Novice, expert, and partner profiles for different user needs

## Quick Start

```bash
DMARCREPORT_API_KEY=your-key npx @duocircle/dmarcreport-mcp
```

> **Need an API key?** See the [API Token Setup Guide](https://support.dmarcreport.com/support/solutions/articles/5000873350-api-tokens) to generate one from your DMARCReport account.

## Installation

This MCP server works with any AI assistant that supports the Model Context Protocol.

### Claude Desktop

Add to your Claude Desktop configuration:

**macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
**Windows:** `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "dmarcreport": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@duocircle/dmarcreport-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "DMARCREPORT_API_KEY": "your-api-key",
        "DMARCREPORT_PROFILE": "novice"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Claude Code (CLI)

Add to `~/.claude.json`:

```json
